      "response": {
        "category": "correctness",
        "consequence": "Existing Disqus import workflows that rely on `-c` break. Imported topics lose their original chronology and category placement.",
        "evidence_refs": [
          "source:new:lib/tasks/disqus.thor@sha256:f1e3eae78c2e27f951d8626fc51de67bd82d75369092c145cf9fe75174f50253",
          "source:old:lib/tasks/disqus.thor@sha256:deb672af79eedceea360dd99e16c608b13d550af224d6ab4ce7f6a4048fb5d6d"
        ],
        "explanation": "The change removes the `--category` method_option and the category lookup. It also removes the `created_at: Date.parse(t[:created_at])` argument that the old PostCreator call passed. Topics are now created through `TopicEmbed.import_remote(user, t[:link], title: t[:title])`, which has no category and no created_at. Running `disqus import -c Comments` now fails with Thor's unknown-option handling, or silently ignores the option. Imported topics land in the default category, stamped with the import time instead of the Disqus thread time.",
        "lines": {
          "end_line": 148,
          "start_line": 148
        },
        "other_findings": [
          {
            "category": "persistence_migration",
            "consequence": "Possible loss of stored topic_embeds or top_topics data when the migration is re-run.",
            "evidence_refs": [
              "source:new:db/migrate/20131217174004_create_topic_embeds.rb@sha256:d3838c0471d17c40f97792cd5bdf1a5f2ac0bab0e6509f202553eadc50dd65f9",
              "source:new:db/migrate/20131223171005_create_top_topics.rb@sha256:0476427f7adc6b711218afbdc557f51c229ead28b1ef6df288943f2b1b387c48"
            ],
            "explanation": "Both `create_topic_embeds` (line 3) and `create_top_topics` (the change adds `force: true` to the existing migration) use `force: true`. This issues DROP TABLE IF EXISTS before creating the table. If either migration is re-run, or the table already exists, all rows are silently destroyed. The `create_top_topics` change edits a migration that may already have been applied.",
            "lines": {
              "end_line": 3,
              "start_line": 3
            },
            "replacement": null,
            "rule_refs": [],
            "severity": "low",
            "target_ids": [
